  "summary_en": "New Zealand Police internal policy governing staff use of generative AI. It requires training, tool approval by ICT and a security and privacy group, human-in-the-loop use, output labelling, a ban on court use without approval, vendor notification, and auditing. It uses a risk-based approach with six-monthly review.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "All staff must complete genAI training before using any tool.",
   "Every genAI tool must be reviewed by ICT and Technology Assurance and approved by the Security and Privacy Reference Group.",
   "Fully automated genAI use without a human in the loop is not permitted; users remain accountable.",
   "genAI outputs must be labelled; court use is barred without prior court approval.",
   "Transcription and translation outputs cannot be used directly as evidence; vendors must notify Police of their genAI use."
  ],
